# Trip Bundles Plan

A "trip bundle" lets a travel agent stitch several existing `trips` rows into one multi-leg tour package that travelers see and book as a single trip. Reuses the existing `trips`, `booking`, and `payments` tables.

## Locked Design Decisions

| # | Topic | Decision |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Membership scope | Bundle members must all belong to the bundling agent (single payout, no cross-agent revenue split for MVP). |
| 2 | Anchor creation | Agent picks legs; backend auto-creates a new `trips` row as the anchor with aggregated fields. |
| 3 | Member trip listings | Member trips remain independently listed; seats are shared (booking the bundle or the leg decrements the same `available_seats`). |
| 4 | Pricing | Pure sum of member `price` values. No discount control in MVP. |
| 5 | Shape | Minimum 2 legs. Both open walks (start ≠ end) and closed walks (start = end) allowed. |
| 6 | Edge uniqueness | Directed — `(origin, destination)` pair must be unique across legs; `A→B` and `B→A` are distinct edges. |
| 7 | Temporal rule | `member[i].arrival_time <= member[i+1].departure_time` (no time travel). No minimum layover enforced. |
| 8 | Edit policy | Fully editable before any booking exists. Immutable after the first confirmed booking on the bundle. |
| 9 | Member-edit propagation | DB trigger recomputes anchor `price`, `total_seats`, `available_seats` when any member changes. |
| 10 | Cancellation | Cancelling a bundle booking refunds in full and increments seats on every member. No partial-leg cancellation. |
| 11 | Member-agent notifications | Reuse `booking_notifications`. Since all legs belong to the same agent (decision 1), one combined notification per bundle booking is sufficient. |
| 12 | Listings UX | Bundles render inline with regular trips using the existing `is_tour_package` "Tour Package" badge already wired into `TripCardFlexible`. |
| 13 | Title | Auto-generated: `"Tour: CityA → CityB → … → CityZ"`. No new column needed. |
| 14 | Geography | Pakistani cities only. Validate on create against the same city list already used by trip creation. |

## Chain Validation Rules (enforced by the bundle create/update API)

Given `legs = [trips[id] for id in member_trip_ids]`:

1. `len(legs) >= 2`
2. All legs have `agent_id == current_agent_id` (decision 1)
3. Continuity: for every `i`, `legs[i].destination_city == legs[i+1].origin_city`
4. Directed-edge uniqueness: `(origin_city, destination_city)` pairs are all distinct
5. Temporal: `legs[i].arrival_time <= legs[i+1].departure_time`
6. Seats: every leg has `available_seats > 0`
7. None of the legs is itself a bundle anchor (no nesting)

