## Phase 1 — Database Migration

Single additive SQL migration. No drops, no renames. Add to `backend/supabase/` as `trip_bundles_member_ids.sql` (or extend the existing additive migration file).

### 1.1 New column on `trips`

```sql
alter table public.trips
  add column if not exists member_trip_ids bigint[] not null default '{}';

create index if not exists idx_trips_member_trip_ids
  on public.trips using gin (member_trip_ids);
```

Semantics:

- Empty array = ordinary single trip (default).
- Non-empty array = bundle anchor; ordered list of member `trip_id`s, leg 1 first.
- The existing `is_tour_package` column should also be set `true` on bundle anchors so `TripCardFlexible` keeps its current badge logic.

### 1.2 Aggregate recompute function and trigger

```sql
create or replace function public.recompute_bundle_anchor(p_anchor_id bigint)
returns void language plpgsql as $$
declare
  v_ids bigint[];
begin
  select member_trip_ids into v_ids from public.trips where trip_id = p_anchor_id;
  if v_ids is null or array_length(v_ids, 1) is null then
    return;
  end if;

  update public.trips a
  set
    price            = (select coalesce(sum(t.price), 0)
                        from public.trips t
                        where t.trip_id = any(v_ids)),
    total_seats      = (select coalesce(min(t.total_seats), 0)
                        from public.trips t
                        where t.trip_id = any(v_ids)),
    available_seats  = (select coalesce(min(t.available_seats), 0)
                        from public.trips t
                        where t.trip_id = any(v_ids)),
    origin_city      = (select t.origin_city
                        from public.trips t
                        where t.trip_id = v_ids[1]),
    destination_city = (select t.destination_city
                        from public.trips t
                        where t.trip_id = v_ids[array_upper(v_ids, 1)]),
    departure_time   = (select t.departure_time
                        from public.trips t
                        where t.trip_id = v_ids[1]),
    arrival_time     = (select t.arrival_time
                        from public.trips t
                        where t.trip_id = v_ids[array_upper(v_ids, 1)]),
    is_tour_package  = true
  where a.trip_id = p_anchor_id;
end;
$$;

create or replace function public.trg_member_trip_changed()
returns trigger language plpgsql as $$
declare
  anchor_id bigint;
begin
  for anchor_id in
    select trip_id from public.trips
    where new.trip_id = any(member_trip_ids)
  loop
    perform public.recompute_bundle_anchor(anchor_id);
  end loop;
  return new;
end;
$$;

drop trigger if exists trg_member_trip_aggregates on public.trips;
create trigger trg_member_trip_aggregates
after update of price, total_seats, available_seats, origin_city, destination_city,
                departure_time, arrival_time on public.trips
for each row execute function public.trg_member_trip_changed();
```

### 1.3 Protect member trips from deletion while bundled

```sql
create or replace function public.trg_block_member_delete()
returns trigger language plpgsql as $$
begin
  if exists (
    select 1 from public.trips
    where old.trip_id = any(member_trip_ids)
  ) then
    raise exception 'Trip % is a member of an active bundle and cannot be deleted', old.trip_id;
  end if;
  return old;
end;
$$;

drop trigger if exists trg_member_trip_delete_guard on public.trips;
create trigger trg_member_trip_delete_guard
before delete on public.trips
for each row execute function public.trg_block_member_delete();
```

### 1.4 Update schema documentation

After applying the migration, update `.cursor/rules/database-schema.mdc` to list the new `trips.member_trip_ids` column and the two new triggers under the trips table section.

