## Phase 2 — Application Development

### 2.1 Backend (`backend/app/api/trips.py`)

- Add `member_trip_ids: List[int] = []` to `TripCreate` and `TripResponse` Pydantic models.
- New endpoint `POST /api/trips/bundle` that accepts `{ member_trip_ids: [int, ...] }` and:
  1. Verifies all member IDs belong to the calling agent.
  2. Loads the member rows, then runs the seven Chain Validation Rules above.
  3. Inserts the anchor row with aggregated fields, `member_trip_ids` populated, `is_tour_package = true`, `agent_id = current_agent_id`.
  4. Returns the new anchor in the standard `TripResponse` shape.
- New endpoint `PATCH /api/trips/bundle/{anchor_id}` for pre-booking edits. Reject if any non-cancelled `booking` row references this anchor.
- Extend `DELETE /api/trips/{id}` to also reject deletion of an anchor if it has any non-cancelled booking; otherwise allow.
- New endpoint `GET /api/trips/{id}/legs` returning the ordered member rows for bundle anchors.

### 2.2 Backend (`backend/app/api/bookings.py`)

- In `create_booking` (~line 448), after fetching the trip:
  - If `trip.member_trip_ids` is non-empty, treat as bundle:
    - Fetch all member rows in one query.
    - Validate every member has `available_seats >= number_of_seats`.
    - In a transaction: decrement `available_seats` on every member and the anchor; insert one `booking` row pointing at the anchor; insert one `payments` row for the summed total.
    - Insert one `booking_notifications` row for the traveler.
    - Insert one notification for the bundling agent summarizing all legs.
- In `cancel_booking`:
  - If the booked trip is a bundle anchor, increment `available_seats` on every member and the anchor in one transaction. Refund logic is unchanged.

### 2.3 Frontend additions

- The tour-package builder lives at `frontend/src/pages/ResourceInventory.tsx` (the old
  mock bus/hotel page was retired). It is the **only** page where bundles are created;
  there is no separate `CreateBundle.tsx` file.
  - Left panel: agent's own active trips (uses existing `getMyTrips`).
  - Right panel: ordered "Stop N" cards with up/down/remove buttons.
  - **Journey map** card at the top renders `BundleRouteMap` (see 2.4) live as stops are added.
  - Live validator surfacing the failing rule in plain English (continuity / duplicate
    edge / time-travel / seat shortage). On submit calls `POST /api/trips/bundle`.
- `frontend/src/components/TripCardFlexible.tsx`:
  - When `trip.member_trip_ids?.length >= 2`, render `"A {N}-stop guided journey"`
    beneath the existing "Tour Package" badge.
- `frontend/src/pages/TripDetails.tsx`:
  - If the trip is a bundle anchor, fetch `GET /api/trips/{id}/legs`, render
    `BundleRouteMap` with all stops, then a customer-facing accordion ("Stop N · A → B",
    Travel by / Departs / Arrives / Travel partner). No internal trip IDs are shown.
- `frontend/src/pages/MyBookings.tsx`:
  - For bookings whose embedded `trip.member_trip_ids.length >= 2`, render a
    "Tour Package · N stops" chip and an expandable itinerary panel with one row per stop.
- `frontend/src/lib/api.ts`:
  - `member_trip_ids?: number[]` on `TripResponse`.
  - `createBundle(memberTripIds)`, `updateBundle(anchorId, memberTripIds)`,
    `getBundleLegs(anchorId)` helpers.

### 2.4 Routing, access, and map visualization

- Agent sidebar entry **"Tour Packages"** (`/agent/resource-inventory`, Sparkles icon).
- There is no `/agent/bundles/new` route — the same URL slot that used to host the mock
  Resource Inventory now hosts the tour-package builder.
- `frontend/src/components/BundleRouteMap.tsx` provides the map visualization:
  - Built on `react-leaflet` + CARTO Voyager tiles (free, no API key).
  - City coordinates come from `frontend/src/lib/pakistanCities.ts`.
  - Numbered gradient pins (emerald = start, indigo = mid, amber = end) plus an animated
    dashed flowing polyline (CSS keyframes `bundle-route-flow` in `index.css`).
  - Renders a "Continuous journey" banner overlay when ≥ 2 stops are present.
- The map appears in two places: the journey builder (live) and TripDetails (traveler view).

### 2.5 Testing

- Manual flow: create 4 PK trips for one agent → create a bundle KHI→LHE→ISB→KHI → confirm anchor row appears in traveler home with "Tour Package" badge → book the bundle → verify seats decrement on all 4 legs and one `booking` row exists → cancel → verify seats restored.
- Add the scenarios above to `TESTING_GUIDE.md` as a new section "8) Trip Bundles".

---

## Out of Scope (deferred)

- Cross-agent bundles and revenue split.
- Bundle discount or free-form pricing.
- Partial leg cancellation.
- Bundle nesting (a bundle that contains another bundle as a leg).
- Non-Pakistani routes.
- A separate "Tour Packages" tab on the traveler home (bundles render mixed in for now).
